    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "theme.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Change only parse_hex_color. Trim the text with trim before strip_prefix. Do not remove spaces that sit inside the hex. Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch decode_channels or high_byte. The existing test bad_color_is_an_error_not_black stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_theme_color_may_have_outer_spaces uses editor_color_theme. BackgroundColor of space, #ffffff is opaque white. BackgroundColor of #ffffff, space is opaque white. BackgroundColor of #ff, space, ff is still an error. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
